WEBVTT

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:21.450
<b>Muhyo & Roji's
Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.490
Where did you find that?

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.610
In the library. Some 
creepy-looking guy dropped it.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.120
Actually...

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.410
He looked just like that.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.510
<b>Article 5 
Insanity</b>

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:03.010
We were all classmates at MLS.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.520
We hung out together all the time.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:10.410
C'mon, you guys!

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.740
Hurry up!

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.530
The colonel's really scary when you're late!

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.400
Well, that sounds like a pain.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.160
Jeez! We're late because you 
wouldn't wake up, Muhyo!

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.740
Question for the three who were late!

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.610
On this sheet is a magical law diagram.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:33.500
This is a mission to free a home that's 
been occupied by five spirits!

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.280
Use these two pieces, the first-class 
secretary and the executor,

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.510
to complete the mission!

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.510
If you fail, you'll get no dinner tonight!

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.450
So, do you understand this?

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.860
Not a clue.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.340
Oh, man! My dinner!

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.500
The mission...

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.640
is complete.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.850
Well done! Truly commendable work!

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.350
Wow! Awesome!

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:34.360
Way to go, Enchu! You're a genius!

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.240
Now our dinner is saved.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.840
Hey, Enchu!

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.480
Let's play!

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.780
You're such a kid.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.790
Sorry, I can't today.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.270
<i>Enchu was constantly studying.</i>

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.040
<i>He wanted to become an executor early</i>

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.920
<i>so he could help his poor 
family and his sick mother.</i>

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.300
He was always saying that.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:00.090
Jabin

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.720
Study?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.770
Hmph. Why should I?

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:06.350
I just thought it's a waste of
 your talent otherwise.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.700
I can tell you're really capab—

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.480
Run! It's a spirit!

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.200
Let me eat you...

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.630
Yoichi!

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.740
Jabin

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:37.210
Magic Binding Spell!

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:41.540
Huh?

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:46.000
C-Curses!

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.780
Hurry up and call an executor.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.100
This is more than we can handle.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.890
R-Right. Got it!

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.790
Muhyo, you can use the pen...

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.080
Since when?

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.090
It was just a fluke.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.900
Pretty good for my first time using it, huh?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.780
A fluke?

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:12.120
Jabin

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.400
That's a lie.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.460
Wow, really?!

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.840
You guys might be chosen as executors?!

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.670
It's true, but the bad news is...

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.750
It can only be one of us.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.680
Let him have it! You don't 
want the job anyway, right?

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:32.360
Shut up. They said I don't 
get to make that choice.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.200
Aw, come on!

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:37.450
Don't tease us.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.710
I'm serious about this.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.820
O-Okay...

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.560
Let's see...

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.020
Oh, right.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.200
Darn it...

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.490
Hey, Muhyo.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.240
You should study a little, too.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.370
Enchu's been awake for 
three days as of yesterday.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.850
Hmph. I'll die before you catch 
me pulling an all-nighter.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:43.290
Huh?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.090
Hey, you're studying right now.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.290
Shut up.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:51.850
Enchu?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.180
Just wait, Mom! I'll be an executor soon!

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.840
I swear I'll make you happy!

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.520
Hey, kid!

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.750
You need to buy a ticket!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:07.610
Mom! Mom!

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:07.210
Kid...

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:11.340
Mom!

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.120
Mother in critical condition

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.410
Soratsugu

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.660
Come back

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:19.830
Urgent Telegram 
Mother in critical condition 
Soratsugu  Come back

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.620
I can't refuse?

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.460
We appreciate that sense of friendship,

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.660
Executor Muhyo.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:36.470
Celebrating the New Executor, Muhyo

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.230
<b>Executor</b>

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.520
<b>Muhyo</b>

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.650
<b>Muhyo</b>

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.420
Congratulations!

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.790
You really pulled it off!

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.550
Where's Enchu?

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.130
Oh. Haven't seen him since he ran off.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:14.760
He probably doesn't know.

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:28.010
Banzai! Good for you, Muhyo!

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:47.880
As dense as I am, I didn't notice 
how weird Enchu was acting.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.860
Of course, even if I had,

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.630
I doubt I would've been able 
to stop what he did next.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.660
He caused the worst disaster 
in the history of magical law.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.550
He's still trying to 
destroy the Association,

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:05.140
as well as Muhyo and the rest of us.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:11.110
Wait, why is there someone on the roof?

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.740
What's this? Is it snowing?

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.870
Long live Muhyo!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:34.000
<i>Enchu had already lost his mind by then.</i>

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.880
<i>His deep sorrow and hatred broke him.</i>

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:49.910
What are those?!

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:51.320
Are they spirits?

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.530
Run!

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.000
What is that?!

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.620
A spirit?!

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.530
They just keep coming!

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:10.880
What do we do, Muhyo-san?!

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.380
Hey, Enchu.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.460
Good luck, Muhyo.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:30.020
<b>Spirit Striker</b>

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.020
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:36.030
<b>Beelzebub's Treasure Chest</b>

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:36.030
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.530
Good luck, Muhyo.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.510
So that's Enchu?

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:45.040
Huh?

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.540
He's gone!

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:49.770
Hey.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.540
It's been a long time, Muhyo.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.420
And it's nice to meet you,

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:58.800
Nana-san.

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:02.360
What?! How did you get in here?!

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.550
And how do you know my name?!

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:08.180
So, how's the power of the dark side?

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.560
Does it feel good?

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:10.840
Actually,

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:13.810
it was so painful...

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:18.460
being unable to tell you 
how wonderful it is.

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:26.490
They're vengeful spirits!

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.420
Huh? Vengeful spirits?!

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:31.080
They're all over town!

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:36.340
The only one capable of this is...

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:37.420
Enchu.

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.090
He must be where Muhyo is!

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:40.840
What?!

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:42.840
This is really bad!

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.160
You know, Enchu...

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.350
Controlling spirits for too long

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.890
brings you closer to 
being a spirit yourself.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:52.850
You're okay with that?

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:56.610
Yes, if it lets me destroy you.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:00.040
I see.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.610
That sounds just like something

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:04.990
an ordinary guy like you would come up with.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.040
Muhyo, don't die too quickly.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:22.660
He vanished?

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:24.010
Cover your ears.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:24.860
Huh?

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:25.720
It'll kill you.

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:34.060
Everyone, cover your ears!

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.700
<b>Go help Muhyo</b>

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.020
Hurry!

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:54.460
Yoichi-san?

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.960
In the name of Judge Himukai Yoichi,

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.220
I enforce the...

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.300
Magic Binding Spell!

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:14.520
Yoichi-san!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.910
Are you okay?

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:20.090
Hey! Why are you still here?!

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:20.890
Huh?

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:23.260
Why aren't you with Muhyo?!

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:26.660
Because you'd be far more 
helpful to him than I would...

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.330
Don't you know?

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:31.160
It's common knowledge in magical law

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:34.200
that the only ones who can be 
assistants to executors are judges.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:36.970
That's because we judges

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:41.170
are experts who've mastered all 
magical law outside of the executive!

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.940
And yet, Muhyo chose you.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:48.360
I wanted to team up with 
him, but he chose you.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:53.140
He chose you as his partner 
in the uphill battle

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:56.180
he knew he'd be facing as Enchu's target!

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:00.280
Huh? I don't need to cover my ears anymore?

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:04.900
With this many, just covering 
your ears isn't enough.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:09.670
I put up Silver Armor, but we're 
not gonna get anywhere this way.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:13.790
Tsk, that idiot. Of all the times...

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:17.690
You're the one he needs by his 
side most when he's in trouble!

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.040
So why aren't you there?!

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:22.290
Be proud, Roji! You are...

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:25.350
the assistant to the genius Muhyo Toru!

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.090
Muhyo...

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:28.810
chose me?

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.690
What's going on here?!

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:41.560
Silver Armor protects humans from 
the screams of vengeful spirits,

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:44.070
but it can't protect the 
surrounding objects.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.060
You mean...

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.780
Ouch...

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.800
Damn you, Enchu...

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:21.190
Magic Binding Spell!

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:33.950
He got them?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.580
Roji-kun!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:41.710
Sorry I'm late.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:46.210
Late as you were, you did 
prove a little bit useful.

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:48.840
I'm sorry, Muhyo.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.820
Save the apologies for later.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.080
It hurts...

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.080
Help...

00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:58.970
Someone...

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.090
What is this?!

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.800
That's the vengeful spirit's original body.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:07.230
This is where the ones in town came from.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:11.500
Enchu gathered a bunch of wandering 
spirits that couldn't move on,

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.240
and sealed them inside this shirt

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.820
so he could call them forth at any time.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:18.900
That lets him produce as many 
of these guys as he wants.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:24.750
Muhyo!

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.500
Hey.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:26.790
I'm leaving them to you.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.500
What?!

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:29.930
That's just...

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:32.760
Oh, no!

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.870
Muhyo!

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:43.600
Help!

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.720
Muhyo!

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.900
You can't even buy a little time?

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:53.900
The only things I've got for you 
guys are tickets straight to Hell.

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:04.350
According to Magical Law Article 1742,

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:08.830
for the crimes of "Attempted Mass Murder" 
and "Unsolicited Object Parasitism"...

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:08.080
<b>Crimes: Attempted Mass Murder and 
Unsolicited Object Parasitism</b>

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.750
<b>Sentence: Hell Train</b>

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:12.840
I sentence you to "Hell Train"!

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:17.190
What is this?!

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:20.220
Way to go, Roji!

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:22.600
No, no, no!

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.800
Is that...

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:52.960
It can't be!

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.840
It's Muhyo's Hell Train.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:58.510
The one that's so powerful, even the 
most renowned executors can't use it?

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.680
<i>That</i> Hell Train?!

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:08.460
Muhyo's won this time.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.570
But you'll be back, won't you, Enchu?

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.570
Looks like the Hell Train's 
gonna be filled to capacity.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:20.320
That's the Hell Train? 
It certainly is impressive.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:25.370
But the only one capable of controlling 
this many vengeful spirits is...

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.600
Enchu?

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:30.640
This battle started out between 
Muhyo-dono and Enchu.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:33.840
Shouldn't we ban Muhyo-dono from this town?

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:36.840
Hey.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:40.580
You're really gonna take <i>that </i>attitude
 toward the one who saved your hides?

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.750
Come, Roji.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:49.950
What happened today

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:54.390
was only a taste of the curses that Enchu 
will deal out to me and the Association.

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:56.570
Can you endure that?

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:57.860
What do you mean?

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:01.200
Enchu will continue to attack,

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.690
and he won't stop unless I drag 
him back from the dark side...

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:07.140
or unless I die.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.080
I have my doubts that you can endure it.

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:15.340
You know what I'm getting at, don't you?

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.850
<i>Is he... saying goodbye?</i>

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:19.840
<i>No!</i>

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:21.610
I'm saying...

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:22.840
<i>Muhyo!</i>

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:25.100
<i>Don't do this!</i>

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:29.100
...that you need to stay close 
to me so you don't get killed.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:33.100
I can't guarantee your life anymore.

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.490
Oh, that's all?

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:39.240
Say what?!

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.240
You were so misleading...

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.780
Muhyo chose you.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:48.060
Don't scare me like that, Muhyo.

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:50.060
You don't have to say all that to me.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.810
Of course I'll follow you.

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:57.250
<i>So you really...</i>

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:00.260
<i>want me to stay at your side, then?</i>

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.740
Muhyo, you jerk!

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:10.720
Can't hear you over the noise.

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.040
Sheesh...

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:17.800
Muhyo!

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:28.540
You earned this rest, Muhyo.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:38.760
The Hell Train is taking
 the vengeful spirits with it.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:41.750
Knowing Muhyo, they're bound for Hell.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.180
Too bad about the exam being postponed.

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:53.370
It's all right. I got to learn 
a lot about Muhyo from you.

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:56.190
I need to get him home, so he can rest.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.190
Oh, really?

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:01.150
Then I guess you don't want 
this specially-issued,

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:06.200
temporary first-class secretary's 
license as a reward for your efforts?

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.700
<b>First-Class Secretary
 Temporary License</b>

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.700
What?!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:12.060
Come on, stop!

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:14.210
Nana-chan!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:18.710
Take care of Muhyo!

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:55.310
Let's learn about magical law!

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:55.310
(with video)

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:55.310
